From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: replace the RX buffer IDR with a table

Every RX buffer gets an id from the ring's IDR when it is posted and gives
it back when it is reaped, and the IDR allocation is one of the larger
costs per received frame. The ids a ring hands out are bounded by the
ring size, so keep them in a table indexed by id with a stack of the free
ones instead. Posting a buffer pops an id and reaping it pushes the id
back, both in constant time under the existing ring lock.

The table holds twice the ring size: a ring never has more buffers posted
than entries, plus the defragmented frames reinjected into the refill
ring. Id 0 stays unused, as with the IDR, because the refill path treats
it as invalid.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
